Yes. Your best bet is to make it to the upstairs before him. IIRC, all 
the named demons will follow you down the stairs, so wait until he is 
next to you, and then go down. You may not end up on the upstairs at the 
first try, however.

>     2> I had Poison Resistance, but still died from Juiblex poisoning me. 
> Why?

Because Juiblex causes sickness which is distinct from poison. Sickness 
can be cured by, among other things, a non-cursed unicorn horn or the 
cure sickness spell. There is also another nasty demon with a sickness 
attack, but let us hope you don't run into him.

>     3> Disenchanters - Anyway to stop them ? 

They can be quite annoying. I usually let my pets deal with them, but 
any ranged attack will do fine. By the time you meet disenchanters you 
should have lots of spare wands, maybe some potent attack spells and 
perhaps even a stack of enchanted daggers. (Of course, I neglected to 
mention that in my current game I'm right next to a disenchanter with 
none of the above, so perhaps I should take my own advice from time to 
time :-)

